{"id":"mahabharata-5-096","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":96,"title":"षण्णवतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 96 · Matali and Narada in Varuna's realm","summary":{"en":"On his way Matali meets Narada, who is going to visit Varuna, and the two go together. Narada shows him the wonders of Varuna's watery realm, with its weapons, treasures and the abode of the moon's radiance, but Matali finds no suitable bridegroom there.","kn":"ದಾರಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ವರುಣನನ್ನು ಕಾಣಲು ಹೋಗುತ್ತಿದ್ದ ನಾರದರನ್ನು ಮಾತಲಿ ಭೇಟಿಯಾಗುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಇಬ್ಬರೂ ಒಟ್ಟಿಗೆ ಹೋಗುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಆಯುಧ, ಸಂಪತ್ತು, ಚಂದ್ರಕಾಂತಿಯ ನೆಲೆ ಇರುವ ವರುಣನ ಜಲಲೋಕದ ಅದ್ಭುತಗಳನ್ನು ನಾರದರು ತೋರಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಆದರೆ ಮಾತಲಿಗೆ ಅಲ್ಲಿ ಯೋಗ್ಯ ವರ ಸಿಗುವುದಿಲ್ಲ.","hi":"मार्ग में मातलि नारद से मिलते हैं, जो वरुण से मिलने जा रहे हैं, और दोनों साथ चलते हैं। नारद उन्हें वरुण के जलमय लोक के आश्चर्य दिखाते हैं, उसके अस्त्र, खज़ाने और चन्द्रमा की कान्ति का निवास, पर मातलि को वहाँ कोई योग्य वर नहीं मिलता।","te":"దారిలో వరుణుని చూడడానికి వెళ్తున్న నారదుని మాతలి కలుస్తాడు, ఇద్దరూ కలిసి వెళ్తారు. ఆయుధాలు, సంపదలు, చంద్రకాంతి నివాసం ఉన్న వరుణుని జలలోకపు అద్భుతాలను నారదుడు చూపిస్తాడు, కానీ మాతలికి అక్కడ తగిన వరుడు దొరకడు.","ta":"வழியில் வருணனைக் காணச் செல்லும் நாரதரை மாதலி சந்திக்க, இருவரும் சேர்ந்து செல்கிறார்கள். ஆயுதங்கள், செல்வங்கள், சந்திர ஒளியின் இருப்பிடம் உள்ள வருணனின் நீருலக அதிசயங்களை நாரதர் காட்டுகிறார், ஆனால் மாதலிக்கு அங்குத் தகுந்த மணமகன் கிடைக்கவில்லை.","ml":"വഴിയിൽവെച്ച് വരുണനെ സന്ദർശിക്കാൻ പോകുന്ന നാരദനെ മാതലി കാണുന്നു; ഇരുവരും ഒരുമിച്ച് പോകുന്നു. ആയുധങ്ങളും നിധികളും, ചന്ദ്രപ്രഭയുടെ വാസസ്ഥലവും ഉൾപ്പെടെ വരുണന്റെ ജലലോകത്തെ അദ്ഭുതങ്ങൾ നാരദൻ കാണിച്ചുകൊടുക്കുന്നു; എങ്കിലും അവിടെ യോഗ്യനായ വരനെ മാതലി കണ്ടെത്തുന്നില്ല."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.96; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"भगवद्यानपर्व","titleEn":"Bhagavadyana Parva (Krishna's embassy)","verses":[{"text":"कण्व उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Kanva said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"मातलिस्तु व्रजन्मार्गे नारदेन महर्षिणा ।\nवरुणं गच्छता द्रष्टुं समागच्छद्यदृच्छया ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Matali went along the road, by chance he met the great sage Narada, who was going to see Varuna."}},{"n":2,"text":"नारदोऽथाब्रवीदेनं क्व भवान्गन्तुमुद्यतः ।\nस्वेन वा सूत कार्येण शासनाद्वा शतक्रतोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Narada then said to him: Where are you going, charioteer? On your own errand or by the command of Indra?"}},{"n":3,"text":"मातलिर्नारदेनैवं संपृष्टः पथि गच्छता ।\nयथावत्सर्वमाचष्ट स्वकार्यं वरुणं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Questioned thus on the road by Narada, Matali told him everything truthfully about his own errand to Varuna."}},{"n":4,"text":"तमुवाचाथ स मुनिर्गच्छावः सहिताविति ।\nसलिलेशदिदृक्षार्थमहमप्युद्यतो दिवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sage said to him: Let us go together; I too have set out from heaven, wishing to see the lord of the waters."}},{"n":5,"text":"अहं ते सर्वमाख्यास्ये दर्शयन्वसुधातलम् ।\nदृष्ट्वा तत्र वरं कंचिद्रोचयिष्याव मातले ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall tell you everything while showing you the earth's depths; and when we see some groom there, Matali, we shall choose him."}},{"n":6,"text":"अवगाह्य ततो भूमिमुभौ मातलिनारदौ ।\nददृशाते महात्मानौ लोकपालमपां पतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then both Matali and Narada dived into the earth and saw the great-souled guardian of the world, lord of waters."}},{"n":7,"text":"तत्र देवर्षिसदृशीं पूजां प्राप स नारदः ।\nमहेन्द्रसदृशीं चैव मातलिः प्रत्यपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"There Narada received honor like that for a divine sage, and Matali received honor like that for Mahendra."}},{"n":8,"text":"तावुभौ प्रीतमनसौ कार्यवत्तां निवेद्य ह ।\nवरुणेनाभ्यनुज्ञातौ नागलोकं विचेरतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Both glad, they told him their errands, and with Varuna's leave went about the world of the Nagas."}},{"n":9,"text":"नारदः सर्वभूतानामन्तर्भूमिनिवासिनाम् ।\nजानंश्चकार व्याख्यानं यन्तुः सर्वमशेषतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Narada, knowing all the beings who dwell within the earth, explained everything completely to the charioteer."}},{"text":"नारद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Narada said:"}},{"n":10,"text":"दृष्टस्ते वरुणस्तात पुत्रपौत्रसमावृतः ।\nपश्योदकपतेः स्थानं सर्वतोभद्रमृद्धिमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dear Matali, you have seen Varuna surrounded by sons and grandsons; behold the lord of waters' abode, all-auspicious and rich."}},{"n":11,"text":"एष पुत्रो महाप्राज्ञो वरुणस्येह गोपतेः ।\nएष तं शीलवृत्तेन शौचेन च विशिष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is the very wise son of Varuna, lord of cattle; he excels in character, conduct and purity."}},{"n":12,"text":"एषोऽस्य पुत्रोऽभिमतः पुष्करः पुष्करेक्षणः ।\nरूपवान्दर्शनीयश्च सोमपुत्र्या वृतः पतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is his dear son Pushkara, lotus-eyed, handsome and good to see, chosen as husband by the Moon's daughter."}},{"n":13,"text":"ज्योत्स्नाकालीति यामाहुर्द्वितीयां रूपतः श्रियम् ।\nआदित्यस्यैव गोः पुत्रो ज्येष्ठः पुत्रः कृतः स्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The one they call Jyotsnakali, second in beauty and splendor; she is said to be the eldest son of Aditya's Go, made his eldest."}},{"n":14,"text":"भवनं पश्य वारुण्या यदेतत्सर्वकाञ्चनम् ।\nयां प्राप्य सुरतां प्राप्ताः सुराः सुरपतेः सखे ॥","meaning":{"en":"See the house of Varuni, all of gold; having obtained her, the gods became gods, O friend of the lord of gods."}},{"n":15,"text":"एतानि हृतराज्यानां दैतेयानां स्म मातले ।\nदीप्यमानानि दृश्यन्ते सर्वप्रहरणान्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Matali, these are the gleaming weapons of the Daityas who lost their kingdoms, all manner of arms."}},{"n":16,"text":"अक्षयाणि किलैतानि विवर्तन्ते स्म मातले ।\nअनुभावप्रयुक्तानि सुरैरवजितानि ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"These are said to be inexhaustible, passing from hand to hand, wielded by power and won by the gods."}},{"n":17,"text":"अत्र राक्षसजात्यश्च भूतजात्यश्च मातले ।\nदिव्यप्रहरणाश्चासन्पूर्वदैवतनिर्मिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here, Matali, were races of rakshasas and of beings, with divine weapons, made by the earlier gods."}},{"n":18,"text":"अग्निरेष महार्चिष्माञ्जागर्ति वरुणह्रदे ।\nवैष्णवं चक्रमाविद्धं विधूमेन हविष्मता ॥","meaning":{"en":"This fire of great flame burns watchfully in Varuna's lake; the discus of Vishnu was fixed in it, smokeless, fed with offerings."}},{"n":19,"text":"एष गाण्डीमयश्चापो लोकसंहारसंभृतः ।\nरक्ष्यते दैवतैर्नित्यं यतस्तद्गाण्डिवं धनुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is the bow made of Gandi wood, formed for the destruction of the worlds, always guarded by the gods; hence it is called the Gandiva bow."}},{"n":20,"text":"एष कृत्ये समुत्पन्ने तत्तद्धारयते बलम् ।\nसहस्रशतसंख्येन प्राणेन सततं ध्रुवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When a task arises, this bears that strength, steadily with a hundred thousand lives."}},{"n":21,"text":"अशास्यानपि शास्त्येष रक्षोबन्धुषु राजसु ।\nसृष्टः प्रथमजो दण्डो ब्रह्मणा ब्रह्मवादिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"This punishment, the first-born, created by Brahma, the speaker of Brahman, rules even those who cannot be ruled, kings who are friends of rakshasas."}},{"n":22,"text":"एतच्छत्रं नरेन्द्राणां महच्छक्रेण भाषितम् ।\nपुत्राः सलिलराजस्य धारयन्ति महोदयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is the great umbrella of kings, spoken of by Indra; the sons of the lord of the waters bear it with great success."}},{"n":23,"text":"एतत्सलिलराजस्य छत्रं छत्रगृहे स्थितम् ।\nसर्वतः सलिलं शीतं जीमूत इव वर्षति ॥","meaning":{"en":"This umbrella of the king of waters stands in the umbrella-house, and cool water rains all around from it as from a cloud."}},{"n":24,"text":"एतच्छत्रात्परिभ्रष्टं सलिलं सोमनिर्मलम् ।\nतमसा मूर्छितं याति येन नार्छति दर्शनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Water falling from this umbrella, pure like the moon, becomes confused with darkness, so that no sight can be had."}},{"n":25,"text":"बहून्यद्भुतरूपाणि द्रष्टव्यानीह मातले ।\nतव कार्योपरोधस्तु तस्माद्गच्छाव माचिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Matali, there are many wonderful sights to be seen here, but your errand is waiting; therefore let us go on without delay."}}]}]}